00:41:24.850 --> 00:41:29.250
Do you remember that opening sequence where they go and find Tom Berenger,

867
00:41:29.430 --> 00:41:32.430
and he's like face down with some booze?

868
00:41:32.550 --> 00:41:34.230
No one else remember Major League?

869
00:41:34.370 --> 00:41:34.750
Come on!

870
00:41:34.950 --> 00:41:35.710
No, I do, and yes.

871
00:41:35.890 --> 00:41:36.430
Thank you.

872
00:41:36.890 --> 00:41:38.410
Wasn't it exactly the same?

873
00:41:38.550 --> 00:41:38.710
Yes.

874
00:41:38.930 --> 00:41:39.310
Thank you.

875
00:41:39.790 --> 00:41:44.370
Well, I noticed that Steve's face was all scruffy when he wakes up.

876
00:41:44.550 --> 00:41:45.710
He's been on a bender.

877
00:41:46.200 --> 00:41:47.450
He's not making good choices.

878
00:41:48.050 --> 00:41:51.810
Well, Randy said that in order to get that scruffy look,

879
00:41:51.970 --> 00:41:54.010
they had to put a note on the call sheet

880
00:41:54.510 --> 00:41:56.970
reminding him not to shave before coming to work

881
00:41:56.970 --> 00:41:59.450
because Steve would always shave before coming to work.

882
00:41:59.670 --> 00:42:01.850
And they had a little note that said, Steve, don't shave.

883
00:42:02.010 --> 00:42:02.630
Don't shave.

884
00:42:03.110 --> 00:42:04.170
I have a question.

885
00:42:04.430 --> 00:42:05.090
What is it?

886
00:42:05.150 --> 00:42:07.950
What was Michael's budget for this movie?

887
00:42:09.030 --> 00:42:12.670
I don't know, but he made it over a very long period of time.

888
00:42:12.830 --> 00:42:14.830
He did, but we're about to be in the Oval Office.

889
00:42:14.830 --> 00:42:16.830
We've already seen what his condo looks like.

890
00:42:16.970 --> 00:42:20.410
It's candelabras and silver trays and whatnot.

891
00:42:20.590 --> 00:42:24.830
But this Oval Office, which is supposed to be, I'm guessing, the conference room.

892
00:42:24.970 --> 00:42:26.710
Yes, it is the conference room,

893
00:42:26.770 --> 00:42:29.650
and you can even see reception through the door

894
00:42:29.650 --> 00:42:32.990
when the shot is on Michael and Dwight.

895
00:42:33.230 --> 00:42:36.330
Or, I'm sorry, on Michael and Samuel.

896
00:42:36.710 --> 00:42:37.110
Samuel.

897
00:42:37.450 --> 00:42:41.590
Did you see what was outside the window behind President Jackson?

898
00:42:41.910 --> 00:42:42.270
What?

899
00:42:43.950 --> 00:42:45.630
It was amazing.

900
00:42:46.030 --> 00:42:49.130
Our set dressing team was incredible.

901
00:42:49.670 --> 00:42:54.790
I didn't know where we were when the scene started until we reversed the shot,

902
00:42:54.790 --> 00:43:00.550
but they put one of those, like, fakie light box window things behind him.

903
00:43:00.610 --> 00:43:01.350
It was amazing.

904
00:43:01.910 --> 00:43:03.530
Michael put that there.

905
00:43:04.090 --> 00:43:04.650
Yes.

906
00:43:04.810 --> 00:43:08.450
And he hung the elaborate curtains, and he got the sculptures and all the paintings.

907
00:43:09.070 --> 00:43:11.190
Did you catch the address of the White House?

908
00:43:12.050 --> 00:43:13.450
1600 Pennsylvania Avenue?

909
00:43:13.690 --> 00:43:15.830
Washington, D.C., comma, D.C.

910
00:43:16.370 --> 00:43:17.850
Oh, no, I did not.

911
00:43:18.290 --> 00:43:19.610
Washington, D.C., D.C.

912
00:43:22.420 --> 00:43:28.760
Well, in this scene, the president is going to explain that Skarn's old enemy Golden Face

913
00:43:28.760 --> 00:43:34.500
is planning to bomb the NHL All-Star Game, and he's also taken hostages.

914
00:43:34.780 --> 00:43:39.300
Now, this is really personal for the president because he owns the stadium.

915
00:43:39.520 --> 00:43:41.060
It's his retirement plan.

916
00:43:41.220 --> 00:43:41.660
I know.

917
00:43:41.760 --> 00:43:47.600
That's what the president is going to retire doing, is owning this one stadium.

918
00:43:48.560 --> 00:43:54.380
Skarn can't decide if he's going to take this job on or not, so he's got to flip a coin seven times.

919
00:43:54.460 --> 00:43:55.340
Best out of seven.

920
00:43:55.580 --> 00:43:57.320
And he doesn't edit around that.

921
00:43:57.480 --> 00:43:59.500
You're going to see all seven coin flips.

922
00:43:59.720 --> 00:44:00.360
That's right.

923
00:44:01.800 --> 00:44:05.360
So, something BJ said in an interview that I thought was so funny,

924
00:44:05.980 --> 00:44:10.680
because, you know, there is an obsession with all-star games in this movie.

925
00:44:10.680 --> 00:44:18.160
He said he thought that Michael Scott would view an all-star game as the most important event in sports,

926
00:44:18.480 --> 00:44:21.020
even though in real life they're kind of irrelevant.

927
00:44:21.400 --> 00:44:23.440
It's more about the championship game.

928
00:44:23.620 --> 00:44:24.040
Yes.

929
00:44:24.240 --> 00:44:28.260
He said he also liked that Golden Face had a thing for all-star games,

930
00:44:28.300 --> 00:44:33.880
and he had previously blown up the WNBA all-star game, which is how Catherine Zeta Skarn died.

931
00:44:34.160 --> 00:44:38.980
Did anyone else catch it four minutes and ten seconds that Daryl is clean-shaven?

932
00:44:39.320 --> 00:44:39.960
I did.

933
00:44:39.960 --> 00:44:40.500
Mm-hmm.

934
00:44:40.760 --> 00:44:44.440
It's the first time we've seen Daryl without facial hair.

935
00:44:44.920 --> 00:44:45.460
Ever.

936
00:44:45.660 --> 00:44:46.760
In an episode of The Office.

937
00:44:46.960 --> 00:44:47.080
Yeah.

938
00:44:47.720 --> 00:44:50.200
We got a fan question from Pieter G.

939
00:44:50.340 --> 00:44:51.820
in Poland who said,

940
00:44:52.440 --> 00:44:59.800
did the writers have to plan out a theoretical timeline for Michael's film schedule so that hair and wardrobe could represent it?

941
00:44:59.940 --> 00:45:04.320
For example, in addition to the fact that Daryl is clean-shaven,

942
00:45:04.600 --> 00:45:08.800
I noticed that we see Jim and Pam's season one and two hairstyle.

943
00:45:08.800 --> 00:45:11.100
Kelly has her up-do.

944
00:45:11.360 --> 00:45:11.580
Oh, yeah.

945
00:45:12.040 --> 00:45:14.580
Angela has her braid from the early days.

946
00:45:14.940 --> 00:45:18.880
I can only imagine the amount of planning and wardrobe meetings.

947
00:45:18.880 --> 00:45:20.060
Oh, yes.

948
00:45:20.160 --> 00:45:21.040
This was a whole thing.

949
00:45:21.260 --> 00:45:27.560
Just speaking of Daryl, Randy said that we had to pick up some Daryl work from a previous episode,

950
00:45:27.560 --> 00:45:34.700
and hair and makeup had to add back a fake mustache goatee for Daryl to match at one point.

951
00:45:34.700 --> 00:45:35.120
Oh, yeah.

952
00:45:35.280 --> 00:45:36.900
Craig talked about this on the DVD commentary.

953
00:45:36.900 --> 00:45:38.460
I think it was a big thing for him.

954
00:45:38.540 --> 00:45:41.900
He did not want to shave, and BJ really insisted on it.

955
00:45:42.060 --> 00:45:49.400
I guess BJ wanted the character that Daryl plays, President Jackson, to be distinct in time from Daryl Philbin.

956
00:45:49.620 --> 00:45:50.040
Mm-hmm.

957
00:45:50.040 --> 00:45:56.100
But that meant he had to get this weird fakie beard in between as they cut back and forth.

958
00:45:56.460 --> 00:46:01.160
BJ also shared that they had to glue sideburns onto his face.

959
00:46:01.320 --> 00:46:02.440
I didn't even notice that.

960
00:46:02.640 --> 00:46:02.880
Yeah.

961
00:46:03.080 --> 00:46:04.740
You know where you can really see it?

962
00:46:04.840 --> 00:46:07.800
Well, first of all, if you go to 1 minute 55 seconds, you can see it.

963
00:46:07.960 --> 00:46:12.300
But then later in the episode, when he's on the ice skating rink, is when I really saw it.

964
00:46:12.500 --> 00:46:13.200
Oh, okay.

965
00:46:13.620 --> 00:46:15.000
Yeah, fakie sideburns.

966
00:46:15.640 --> 00:46:17.480
Well, we all know Michael's going to take the job.

967
00:46:17.620 --> 00:46:19.540
He didn't need to flip the coin seven times.

968
00:46:20.140 --> 00:46:20.360
No.

969
00:46:20.840 --> 00:46:21.980
Clean up on aisle five.

970
00:46:22.120 --> 00:46:23.320
Clean up on aisle five, guys.

971
00:46:23.980 --> 00:46:28.280
We are now going to the stadium where the hostages are being held.

972
00:46:28.440 --> 00:46:28.760
Mm-hmm.

973
00:46:29.420 --> 00:46:31.660
And we meet Golden Face.

974
00:46:31.940 --> 00:46:32.460
Mm-hmm.

975
00:46:32.640 --> 00:46:33.480
Played by Jim.

976
00:46:33.960 --> 00:46:37.400
Also a very giddy John Krasinski, who wanted the gold makeup.

977
00:46:37.400 --> 00:46:39.540
He was excited to become Golden Face.

978
00:46:40.400 --> 00:46:44.940
You have no idea how excited John was to film Threat Level Midnight.

979
00:46:45.000 --> 00:46:46.220
