This location was the same as the funky cat.

1635
01:16:09.340 --> 01:16:11.580
We just used a different side of the bar.

1636
01:16:11.780 --> 01:16:12.680
Oh, yeah.

1637
01:16:12.860 --> 01:16:13.380
So smart.

1638
01:16:13.600 --> 01:16:13.920
Mm-hmm.

1639
01:16:14.600 --> 01:16:20.040
Well, Karen is going to have a talking head saying, why did you single my line out like a million years later?

1640
01:16:20.280 --> 01:16:25.680
And at 13 minutes, four seconds, for my background folks, you will see another cameo callback.

1641
01:16:26.120 --> 01:16:29.320
Dan Gore is exiting the cafe behind Karen's talking head.

1642
01:16:29.620 --> 01:16:31.640
You know, Dan played Karen's baby daddy.

1643
01:16:31.940 --> 01:16:32.380
Yes.

1644
01:16:32.920 --> 01:16:37.240
Didn't he dress as a hot dog in a photo on her desk or something like that?

1645
01:16:37.380 --> 01:16:38.080
That's amazing.

1646
01:16:38.580 --> 01:16:43.960
As the scene continues in the bar, we find out that Skarn is really depressed, you know?

1647
01:16:44.080 --> 01:16:45.560
And Billy is going to cheer him up.

1648
01:16:45.760 --> 01:16:48.880
He tells a random kid in overalls, who is this kid?

1649
01:16:49.940 --> 01:16:52.180
That kid was played by Joshua Reed.

1650
01:16:52.420 --> 01:16:54.420
All I could think of is like, is this a shroot?

1651
01:16:54.660 --> 01:16:58.180
Like, is one of Dwight's nephews or cousins in town?

1652
01:16:58.180 --> 01:17:02.560
Anyway, he tells the little boy to hit G9 on the jukebox.

1653
01:17:03.240 --> 01:17:05.080
It's time to dance the Skarn.

1654
01:17:05.300 --> 01:17:07.480
Oh, we talked about this with BJ.

1655
01:17:07.880 --> 01:17:08.900
It was so fun.

1656
01:17:09.060 --> 01:17:10.180
All you guys are so funny.

1657
01:17:10.320 --> 01:17:12.360
I love all the cameos in the background of this scene.

1658
01:17:12.480 --> 01:17:13.580
We've got the whole warehouse.

1659
01:17:13.580 --> 01:17:18.020
And then we have Leo from Vance Refrigeration, but not Gino.

1660
01:17:18.280 --> 01:17:22.140
I guess in real life, Gene was like, nah, I don't want to do the Skarn.

1661
01:17:22.180 --> 01:17:23.580
Well, Leo's having a good time.

1662
01:17:23.620 --> 01:17:25.420
And we also have Todd Packer.

1663
01:17:25.420 --> 01:17:25.900
Yeah.

1664
01:17:26.500 --> 01:17:29.480
I will tell you, the day we filmed this was such a blaSt.

1665
01:17:29.660 --> 01:17:33.600
We, of course, had to learn the dance and practice it a few times.

1666
01:17:34.180 --> 01:17:38.520
And we also had to figure out how our character would dance, how up for it they would be.

1667
01:17:39.200 --> 01:17:41.780
And I just have such fond memories of this day.

1668
01:17:42.300 --> 01:17:47.720
We had a fan question from Avery G in Idaho who asked, who choreographed the Skarn?

1669
01:17:48.140 --> 01:17:52.400
Well, I'll tell you, first of all, the lyrics were by BJ and the music was by Eve Nelson again.

1670
01:17:52.400 --> 01:17:55.520
And the choreography was by Marianne Kellogg.

1671
01:17:55.960 --> 01:17:58.600
She's done all our choreography on the show, and she's great.

1672
01:17:58.880 --> 01:18:00.360
Well, she was very patient with us.

1673
